            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0141" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Conference/165b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-01T16:00:00-05:00">November 1, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>434. Press reports Eden stated in Parliament today “The United States took the
                    initiative in convoking Nine Power Conference, etc.” <pb facs="0142" n="134"
                        xml:id="pg134"/> and “I feel I ought to make it quite plain that the
                    initiative for holding the Conference in Brussels never came from us at all, but
                    from the United States.”</p>
                <p>Please cable urgently text of what Eden actually said pertinent to these
                    statements.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
